---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import FinancialStatementKey from "../../components/FinancialStatementKey.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/ukgaap/frs104.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Minimum Content of an Interim Report" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Same Accounting Policies as the Annual Financial Statements" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Materiality in the Interim Context" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Worked Example — Interim Materiality Assessment" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Worked Example — Minimum Interim Content" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Critical Judgments" },
        { id: "s10", label: "FRS 104 vs IAS 34 — Comparison" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A condensed snapshot, not a miniature annual report</div><div class="principle">An INTERIM financial report — covering a period SHORTER than a full financial year (typically half-yearly) — serves a genuinely DIFFERENT purpose than the annual accounts: providing an UPDATE on significant events and changes since the last annual report, rather than reproducing a full, standalone set of financial statements. FRS 104 sets out the MINIMUM content and principles for such interim reports, for entities WITHIN the FRS 102/103 suite.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Entities preparing interim reports under the FRS 102/103 framework</div><div class="principle">FRS 104 applies to entities that PREPARE an interim financial report and that otherwise apply FRS 102 (or FRS 103, for insurers) as their annual reporting framework — it does NOT itself REQUIRE any entity to prepare interim reports; that requirement, where it exists, comes from OTHER sources (e.g. a listing rule, loan covenant, or voluntary choice).</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Minimum Content of an Interim Report</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A condensed set of statements, plus selected explanatory notes</div><div class="principle">A COMPLIANT interim report includes, at minimum: a CONDENSED Balance Sheet (SOFP); a condensed Profit and Loss Account (or statement of comprehensive income); a condensed statement of changes in equity; a condensed statement of cash flows; and SELECTED explanatory notes — considerably ABBREVIATED compared to a full annual set of financial statements, focusing on what has CHANGED since the last annual report.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Same Accounting Policies as the Annual Financial Statements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Consistency between interim and annual reporting</div><div class="principle">An entity applies the SAME accounting POLICIES in its interim report as it applies (or will apply) in its ANNUAL financial statements — EXCEPT for policy changes made AFTER the date of the most recent annual financial statements, which would ALSO be reflected in the NEXT annual statements. This ensures genuine CONSISTENCY and COMPARABILITY between interim and annual reporting.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Materiality in the Interim Context</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Materiality assessed relative to the interim period itself</div><div class="principle">MATERIALITY for interim reporting purposes is assessed in relation to the INTERIM period's OWN financial data — NOT by simply extrapolating the entity's ANNUAL materiality threshold — reflecting that an item significant enough to warrant separate disclosure within a SHORTER interim period might not be considered material when judged solely against ANNUAL figures, and vice versa.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Worked Example — Interim Materiality Assessment</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A different materiality lens for a shorter period</div>
      <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: An unusual half-year expense</div><div class="wk-body">A company incurs a £250,000 one-off restructuring charge during its first half-year, against half-year profit before tax of £2,000,000 (compared to a much larger £15,000,000 ANNUAL profit before tax in the prior year).</div><div class="wk-answer">Although £250,000 might NOT be considered material relative to the FULL-YEAR £15,000,000 figure, it represents a MEANINGFUL 12.5% of the HALF-YEAR £2,000,000 profit — assessed against the INTERIM period's OWN scale, the item warrants SEPARATE disclosure in the interim report, even though it might not have triggered separate disclosure in the ANNUAL accounts.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Worked Example — Minimum Interim Content</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A condensed, not comprehensive, set of statements</div>
      <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A half-yearly report's minimum components</div><div class="wk-body">A company preparing its half-yearly report under FRS 104.</div><div class="wk-answer">The report includes a CONDENSED Balance Sheet as at the half-year end, a condensed Profit and Loss Account for the half-year (and the CORRESPONDING half-year of the prior year), a condensed statement of changes in equity, a condensed statement of cash flows, and SELECTED notes — considerably SHORTER than the full annual accounts, but SUFFICIENT to update readers on significant developments since the last annual report.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What FRS 104 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>A statement that the same accounting policies as the annual accounts have been applied (or details of any changes)</span><span>Explanatory notes on significant events and transactions since the last annual report</span><span>Seasonal or cyclical factors affecting interim results, where relevant</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Critical Judgments</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
      <div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Materiality assessment relative to the interim period, distinct from the annual materiality threshold</span></div></div>
      <div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Interim-period estimates (e.g. tax charge, inventory provisions) may be less precise than year-end equivalents, given time and information constraints</span></div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>FRS 104 vs IAS 34 — Comparison</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — FRS 104 vs IAS 34</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">FRS 104</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 34</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Minimum content</span><span>Condensed statements plus selected notes</span><span>Same broad approach — converged</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Materiality basis</span><span>Assessed relative to the interim period</span><span>Same principle — converged</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Accounting policy consistency</span><span>Same policies as annual accounts</span><span>Same principle — converged</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="note">FRS 104 is one of the MORE genuinely converged standards in the "new UK GAAP" suite relative to its IFRS counterpart — reflecting its narrow, largely procedural scope.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every FRS 104 event lands</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Interim report preparation</span><span>All condensed statements</span><span>Same accounting policies as the annual accounts, condensed presentation</span></div>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>FRS 102</span><span>Supplies the accounting policies an interim report must apply consistently</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>FRS 103</span><span>Applies alongside FRS 104 for insurers' interim reports</span></div>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Condensed financial statements</div><div class="glossary-def">Abbreviated versions of the annual financial statements, focusing on updates since the last annual report.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Interim materiality</div><div class="glossary-def">Materiality assessed relative to the interim period's own financial data, rather than by reference to annual figures.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <FinancialStatementKey />

  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.frs104 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
